  {
    "id": "pie-cases/unclosed directive 0",
    "note": "Unclosed `%%{` directives. Core's preprocess ends one at its line end and reports `UNCLOSED_DIRECTIVE` (an error, so v13 rejects the source); v12's directive regex removed the line break after it too, or every line after it. That is core's reading of directives for every type, not a pie lexer rule, so the gate leaves these out (see the spec).",
    "source": "pie\n%%{ never closed\n\"a\": 1"
  },
  {
    "id": "pie-cases/unclosed directive 1",
    "source": "pie\n%%{init: {\n\"a\": 1"
  }
